      "writtenOn": "2024-09-12T20:35:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is somewhat contrived. Sink Caps shall always contain one 5V fixed PDO. It would be reasonable for us to disregard this sink caps message without ever having evaluated the voltage/current. Maybe we want to test the case of an invalid Sink Caps, but another, separate case would be a fixed 5V/1.5A followed by a variable 5V/3A (still a little silly, but valid).",
      "revId": "3e49f287668e4973fa46ae47e49ecc15f76e9056",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ae13aee4_1cf56932",
        "filename": "zephyr/test/pdc/src/pdc_policy/src_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 804,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-16T01:23:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree this is contrived. pdc_dpm.c has a check that the first sink cap is a fixed PDO so this is just meant to exercise that path.  It probably makes sense to remove the check in pdc_dpm.c, but the main PDC thread should have some checks for invalid sink caps.\nI\u0027ll investigate as a follow up.",
      "parentUuid": "55d84ea9_f5c75b32",
      "revId": "3e49f287668e4973fa46ae47e49ecc15f76e9056",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c3aaed9b_86420e5d",
        "filename": "zephyr/test/pdc/src/pdc_policy/src_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 815,
      "author": {
